# Why have you stopped getting better?
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach","b":"gemini:Puck | eager club player, relaxed and good-humoured; never exaggerated"}
prompt: "Why do the same mistakes keep costing you games? What three questions should you ask before every move? Where do you stand today? (a short scored test)"
next: {"title":"What did your opponent's last move do?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/chess-30-days/02-what-did-your-opponent-s-last-move-do.cast"}

## Too fast
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: r1bqkbnr/ppp2ppp/2n5/3pp3/8/4PN2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 1, moves: [Bd3]}
      - {fen: r1bqkbnr/ppp2ppp/2n5/3pp3/8/3BPN2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 1 1, moves: [e4, Bb5, exf3], flip: true}
      - {fen: 3r2k1/ppp2ppp/4q3/8/8/8/PPQ2PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxc7]}
      - {fen: 3r2k1/ppQ2ppp/4q3/8/8/8/PP3PPP/3R2K1 b - - 0 1, moves: [Rxd1#], flip: true}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "Too fast"

A: Most players stuck around a thousand don't lose to brilliant moves. They lose to one move, played too fast.
    draw position

B: That's me. Here I'd just develop: bishop to d3, done.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.4

A: Swap chairs. You're Black now, and that bishop move just gave you something.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win a piece." widget chess line 1 hints ["One pawn can hit two pieces.","The pawn on e5."] themes ["fork"] voice a
        right: Pawn to e4 hits the bishop and the knight at once. Only one of them can escape.
        wrong: Look for one pawn move that attacks two white pieces.

B: Ouch. The bishop runs, and my knight is gone.
    animate plies_shown 3 duration 2.6

    pause 0.4

B: Next game I'm careful. A free pawn on c7,
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

B: and I take it.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.4

A: Black to move again, and that's you.
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Mate in one." widget chess line 1 hints ["Look at White's back rank.","Your rook."] themes ["back rank"] voice a
        right: Rook takes d1, mate. White's own pawns wall the king in.
        wrong: Every white piece left the first rank. Which of your pieces can reach it?

B: Mate. For one pawn.
    point at.ref sq_d1 gesture circle

    pause 0.5

A: Neither punishment was hard to find. Both moves were played without one look at the reply.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.8

B: So I'm just careless?
    point at.ref piece_c2 gesture circle

A: No. You're missing a habit.
    fade position to 0.4

A: Today: why the mistakes repeat,
    text map_why "why" x 900 y 440 font_size 40

A: the habit that stops them,
    text map_habit "the habit" x 900 y 375 font_size 40

A: and a short test of where you stand.
    text map_test "a test" x 900 y 310 font_size 40

## The Three Questions
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 3r2k1/ppp2ppp/4q3/8/8/8/PPQ2PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxd8+, Qe8, Rxe8#]}
      - {fen: r1bq1rk1/pp1pbppp/5n2/2p1n3/4P3/2NP1N2/PPP1BPPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Nxe5]}
      - {fen: r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/3p1n2/2b1p3/1nB1P3/8/PPPPQPPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 0 1, moves: [Nc3, Nxc2+]}
      - {fen: r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/3p1n2/2b1p3/1nB1P3/8/PPPPQPPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 0 1, moves: [d3]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0
    safety: 0
    arrows:
      - {from: e2, to: c2}
sources:
    - id: heisman
      title: Passive vs Basic Hope Chess
      authors: Dan Heisman
      year: 2018
      finding: 'Hope chess: consistently making moves without analysing the opponent''s possible forcing replies (checks, captures and threats), hoping to have a safe answer if one comes.'
      url: https://www.chess.com/article/view/passive-vs-basic-hope-chess

    card title "The Three Questions"

A: Now that you've seen two fast moves, why do the same ones keep happening?
    draw position

A: Back to the rook game, one move before the pawn grab.
    point at.ref piece_c2 gesture circle

B: I looked at my move. The pawn was free, so I took it.
    point at.ref piece_c7 gesture circle

A: You checked your own idea, and hoped for the rest.
    point at.ref piece_c2 gesture tap

A: The coach Dan Heisman calls it hope chess.
    text hope "hope chess" cites ["heisman"] x 900 y 570 font_size 36

A: The cure is three questions before every move: checks, captures, threats.
    text q_checks "checks" x 900 y 440 font_size 40
    text q_captures "captures" x 900 y 375 font_size 40
    text q_threats "threats" x 900 y 310 font_size 40

    erase hope

B: In that order?
    highlight q_checks q_captures q_threats

A: In that order. A check must be answered, so it's the most forcing move there is.
    highlight q_checks

A: And ask them for both sides.
    highlight piece_g1 piece_g8

A: Start with your own checks.
    highlight piece_d1

    ask "Find the check that wins." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first.","The rook on d1."] themes ["back rank"] voice a
        right: Rook takes d8, check. The queen blocks, and the rook takes it: mate.
        wrong: Every check first, even the ones that give something away.

B: I had mate. And I grabbed a pawn.
    point at.ref piece_g8 gesture circle

    pause 0.4

A: Second question: captures.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

A: What would you play here?
    highlight q_captures

B: Pawn to h3. I always play h3, so nothing lands on g4.
    point at.ref sq_h3 gesture tap

A: Look at who guards what first: red counts attackers, green counts defenders.
    animate safety 1 duration 1.2

A: The knight on e5 has one attacker and no defender. It's loose.
    highlight piece_e5

    ask "Take what's free." widget chess line true hints ["Which black piece has no guard?","Your knight on f3."] themes ["hanging piece"] voice a
        right: Knight takes e5. It was attacked once and defended by nothing.
        wrong: Find the red frame, then find what attacks it.

B: I'd have played h3 and never looked.
    animate safety 0 duration 0.8

A: Third question: threats, and this time his.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

A: His knight just jumped to b4.
    highlight q_threats piece_b4

B: Knight to c3. Develop, like the books say.
    point at.ref sq_c3 gesture tap

    quiz "What does the knight on b4 threaten?" voice a
        right: Knight takes c2 with check, and the same knight hits the rook on a1.
        wrong: Look at c2: who guards it, now the queen has left d1?
        + Knight takes c2, check
        * Knight takes a2
        * Nothing yet

A: Play it, and the knight lands on c2.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 2.6

B: Check, and my rook. A fork.
    highlight piece_e1 piece_a1

A: Take it back. Pawn to d3 instead,
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

A: and the queen guards c2.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.4

A: One look at his threat, and the fork never happens.
    draw arrow_0

    erase arrow_0

A: So the mistakes repeat because a habit is missing, not talent:
    fade position to 0.3

A: you look at your move, and hope.
    draw hope

B: Checks, captures, threats. Mine, then his.
    highlight q_checks q_captures q_threats

    erase hope

A: Every move, before your hand touches a piece.
    fade position to 1

## Your turn
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: r5k1/2q3pp/p4p2/8/8/8/PP3PPP/3QR1K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qd5+, Qf7, Qxa8+]}
      - {fen: r1bq1rk1/ppp1bppp/3p1n2/8/2BnP3/2NP1N2/PPP1QPPP/R1B2RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Nxd4]}
      - {fen: rnb2rk1/pp2qppp/2pb1n2/8/3PP3/2NB1N2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [e5]}
      - {fen: r2qk2r/ppp2ppp/2np1n2/2b1p3/2B1P1b1/2NP1N1P/PPP2PP1/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 1, moves: [hxg4]}
      - {fen: r3kb1r/pp3ppp/2n1bn2/3N4/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 1, moves: [Nc7+]}
      - {fen: 4r1k1/2q2ppp/8/8/Q7/2R5/5PPP/6K1 b - - 0 1, flip: true, moves: [Re1#]}
      - {fen: 3r1rk1/p1p1bppp/1pn5/8/8/2PB4/PP2QPPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qe4]}
      - {fen: rnbq1rk1/ppp1bppp/3p1n2/4N3/2B1P3/2NP4/PPP2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 1, flip: true, moves: [dxe5]}
      - {fen: r1bq1rk1/ppp1bppp/3p4/4n3/4P3/1BNP2P1/PPPQ1P1P/R1B2RK1 b - - 0 1, flip: true, moves: [Nf3+]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "Your turn"

A: Now the Three Questions are yours. Three puzzles first: start with checks.
    draw position

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first.","Your queen."] themes ["fork"] voice a
        right: Queen to d5, check, then queen takes a8: one check hit the king and the rook together.
        wrong: Try every check your queen can give, and see what else it hits.

A: Next, a black knight has just landed on d4, hitting your queen.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win a piece." widget chess line true hints ["Captures: which black piece has no guard?","Your knight on f3."] themes ["hanging piece"] voice a
        right: Knight takes d4. It attacked your queen, and nothing defended it.
        wrong: Before you save the queen, count who guards the knight on d4.

B: I'd have moved my queen, and never seen the knight was free.
    point at.ref piece_e2 gesture circle

A: Last one. No good checks, no captures. So look for a threat.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    ask "Win a piece." widget chess line true hints ["One pawn, two targets.","Your e-pawn."] themes ["threat","fork"] voice a
        right: Pawn to e5 attacks the knight and the bishop. One of them falls.
        wrong: Which pawn move attacks two black pieces at once?

A: Now the test: six positions, one move each,
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

A: a mix of what costs games at your level.
    text test_label "Day 1 test" x 900 y 560 font_size 36

A: Take your time. This is your score for today, and day 30 repeats this test.
    highlight test_label effect underline

    ask "Win material." widget chess themes ["hanging piece"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Pawn takes g4: a bishop for a pawn.

A: Number two.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win material." widget chess themes ["fork"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Knight to c7, check: it forks the king and the rook on a8.

A: Three. You're Black for this one.
    animate position_shown 5 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Mate in one." widget chess themes ["back rank"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Rook to e1, mate: the king's own pawns hold him in.

A: Four: White again.
    animate position_shown 6 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win material." widget chess themes ["threat"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Queen to e4 threatens mate on h7 and hits the knight on c6. Black can't stop both.

A: Five, and you're Black.
    animate position_shown 7 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win material." widget chess themes ["hanging piece"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Pawn takes e5: White's knight grabbed a pawn and stood unguarded.

A: Last one, still Black.
    animate position_shown 8 plies_shown 0 duration 0.6

    ask "Win material." widget chess themes ["fork"] line true voice a test day1
        right: Knight to f3, check: it forks the king and the queen on d2.

    erase test_label

    erase position

    text score_big "Day 1 score" x 500 y 400 font_size 110

A: You scored {day1.score} of {day1.total}.
    results test day1

A: Write it down.
    highlight score_big effect underline

B: And if it's low?
    highlight score_big

A: Then it's your starting point, not a verdict.
    erase score_big

A: You stopped improving because you play your move and hope.
    text syn_hope "hope" x 500 y 430 font_size 96

    erase syn_hope

A: Checks, captures, threats, for both sides, turn hope into checking.
    text q_checks "checks" x 500 y 590 font_size 64
    text q_captures "captures" x 500 y 495 font_size 64
    text q_threats "threats" x 500 y 400 font_size 64

A: Homework: play one slow game today, fifteen minutes plus ten or slower,
    text hw_game "one slow game: 15 + 10" x 500 y 265 font_size 48

A: and find its first mistake.
    text hw_mistake "find mistake 1" x 500 y 195 font_size 48

## Where next
end_page: true

Next: What did your opponent's last move do?
    text end_next_kicker "Next" x 500 y 545 font_size 24 style.opacity 0.6
    link end_next href lecture:2 title "What did your opponent's last move do?" size 320 x 500 y 395

    link end_again href lecture:1 title "Watch again" form text open here x 500 y 160
    text end_count "1 of 30" x 500 y 95 font_size 22 style.opacity 0.6
